            <ArticleTitle>The occurrence of the ilio-lumbar syndrome in a spinal cord injury patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>237-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Case report of a 71-year-old man having sustained a spinal cord injury (SCI) for 26 years. He started to suffer from low back pain 21 years after his onset and this was diagnosed as ilio-lumbar syndrome (ILS).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To describe the problem of low back pain occurring after a change of wheelchair in a SCI, and to indicate the importance of the ilio-lumbar syndrome as a possible cause of low back complaint.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OUTCOME" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Clinical findings supported by echotomography confirmed the diagnosis of ILS in our case.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">ILS should be considered when some changes and deterioration of the status of SCI occur due to low back complaint.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
